    <statement><p>Evaluate the iterated integral:</p>
<p><me>\int_{0}^{2} \int_{6}^{7} \sqrt{x+4 y} \,dx \,dy</me>
Answer : <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6.43975</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>y</m> as a constant. Then we evaluate the resulting integral with respect to <m>y</m>:



<me>\begin{array}{l}
\int_{0}^{2}\int_{6}^{7}\sqrt{x+4 y} \,dx \,dy \\
=\int_{0}^{2} \frac{2}{3}{( x+4 y )}^{3/2}\bigg|_{x=6}^{7} \,dy \\
=\int_{0}^{2}\frac{2}{3}\left({( {7}+4 y )}^{3/2}-{( {6}+4 y )}^{3/2}\right)dy  \\
=\frac{2}{3}\left(\frac{2}{5\cdot 4}{( 7+4 y)}^{5/2}
-\frac{2}{5\cdot 4}{( 6+4 y )}^{5/2}\right) \bigg|_{0}^{2} \\
=\frac{1}{15}\left(\left({15}^{5/2}-{14}^{5/2}\right)-\left({7}^{5/2}-{6}^{5/2}\right)\right) \\
=\frac{1}{15}\left({15}^{5/2}-{14}^{5/2}-{7}^{5/2}+{6}^{5/2}\right)\approx 6.43975
\end{array}</me>



</solution>
